#90001
"A Damp Cavern"
"The dank air has caused much moisture to accumulate along the walls, ceilings,

and soggy ground.  Due to the moisture, moss and other fungi have managed to

grow at the intersection of the wall and ground, as well as along parts of the

walls to the north and south.  The cavernous passage seems to open up if you

head west.  To the east, light flickers in the distance, causing shadows to

dance along the walls.

